                "text": "Rep. Roy: \u201cShould we be putting forward legislation that will continue to fund the insurance companies at the level they're currently getting, where 85% of their revenues are coming from the federal government? Because that's what's happening. \n\nOr are the $35 billion going to insure insurance companies last year that go to people that weren't even using their plans? Is that what we should be doing? \n\nIs that the health care system that my colleagues and the other side of the aisle are saying that must be addressed by virtue of subsidies to insurance companies?\u201d",
