                "text": "Rep. Roy on healthcare: \"The American people are getting harmed, unable to afford healthcare, so we shouldn't subsidize insurance companies.\n\nThe average American family spends $25,000 for their insurance between their employer and themselves. They don't get the doctor of their choice. They can't afford to go get healthcare. It is driving up the cost of goods and driving up the cost for small businesses. It's putting people out of business. We need to stop it.\n\nObamacare is broken. Democrats broke it. Republicans should move forward with a strong healthcare freedom plan\u2014empowering doctors and patients, not insurance companies or government bureaucrats.\"",
